// Adjacent to 0904: the same current-request correlation on the left, but
// with NO rigid filter (`C`) — so the `((A S B) ∧ C) ∨ B` rewrite does
// NOT fire (there are no lifted left units) and the backend alone must handle
// the SAME-STEP anchor: at the anchor's own timepoint the left is checked
// over the empty range `(i, i]` and is vacuously true, so the verdict is
// PERMIT regardless of the correlation.
//
// The same-step anchor is the delicate part: an implementation that evaluates
// the anchor subplan separately must still project the correlation column for
// the just-matched anchor row. Projecting it as absent instead makes a strict
// join against the current request's binding reject the row, yielding a wrong
// DENY at @0. In 0904 the rigid `C` made the vacuity disjunct supply the
// row instead, so that shape does not exercise this path.
//
// @10 pins the history path (guard streak for dave holds over (0,1]) and
// @20 is the deny control (dave's event breaks eve's streak).
//
// Expected verdicts are in expected_1.out.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
    since within 1h
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: "carol" }
};
